VIOLATION=entity-precedence-derivation.md COUNT=1
  7:Cycle rule: when `precedes` forms a loop that returns (a walk returns to an entity seen before), the cycle detects a domain. A term that encompasses the cycle must exist as the domain's bracket. That term's `source` points to the anchor concept; its `precedes` points to the cycle start. All cycle members share the same source domain concept.
VIOLATION=system-illustration-scope.md COUNT=1
  5:Illustration must target exactly one pattern (morphism) or one nexus (composition); protocols (entities) and terms target other layers.
VIOLATION=workflow-batch-sequence.md COUNT=1
  3:Scope: task-level. Applies when a task requires two or more distinct aspects. Independent tool calls within one aspect run in parallel; the order constraint bounds aspect transitions and leaves call batches parallel.
